# Rowan's scenes in Maplewood. The format is described at the top of scripts/story.gd.

== rowan_town_chat
@trigger talk rowan
@once
@camera rowan 6
Rowan (neutral): Morning. You're the one who took the Birchfield place.
Nora (worried): Is it that obvious?
Rowan (wry): You've got hay on your sweater and a city coat over it. Small town. We notice.
? What do you say?
- I'm still figuring out which end of a sheep is which. -> honest | trust rowan +2; familiarity rowan +4
- I'll manage. I always do. -> guarded | familiarity rowan +2; set nora_guarded
- Are you always this friendly? -> tease | familiarity rowan +3
@label honest
Rowan (happy): The end that bites is the front. Mostly.
Rowan (warm): Come find me on the hill if they give you trouble. They usually do.
@goto done
@label guarded
Rowan (neutral): Fair enough.
Rowan (warm): Offer stands anyway. The hill, past your fence. If you need a hand.
@goto done
@label tease
Rowan (wry): This is me at my friendliest. Ask Theo.
Nora (happy): I might.
@label done
@set met_rowan
> He tips his head and goes back to watching the road, like he's waiting for something that never comes.
